From 82aa6457ecdefcdb303c7e788154f505dc4b8fc6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 22:58:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10211/11362] Fix the seven writers that kept regenerating
 exp3946's retired substrate

The exp3946 incident class, finished. On 2026-07-27 the exp3946 ARTIFACT was
corrected but its WRITER was not, so every re-run recreated the illegal
inference_substrate. The writer was later fixed -- but SEVEN sibling writers
with the same copy-pasted literal were not, and their artifacts still carry
'offline_arc_agi3_perception_planner_real_env_confirmed' at HEAD:
arc3_r11l_solve, 3954, 3964, 3965, 3966, 3981, 3993 (the known-issues entry
counted 3 because only 3 are lint CANDIDATES; the class is 7 artifacts + 7
writers, re-derived this session).

WRITERS (all seven): now declare
offline_arcade_live_agent_runtime_self_discovery_no_llm, the value exp3946's
own landed correction uses. Verified honest per file before editing: each
constructs Arcade(operation_mode=OperationMode.OFFLINE) and steps the offline
sim; none imports llama/gguf/torch/cuda. Not a relabel past a stricter floor
-- the substrate's floor (0.01s) applies. The bulk of this diff is
hook-mandated: ruff-format refused the commit until the seven legacy files
were reformatted whole; the semantic change per writer is the substrate
literal plus a five-line comment.

ARTIFACTS (four of seven): 3954, 3964, 3965, 3966 corrected with the exp3946
corrigendum pattern (original preserved in
inference_substrate_original_invalid_value + dated correction note); all four
verified fully lint-clean after the edit. The other three artifacts are
DELIBERATELY LEFT UNREPAIRED and reported instead: arc3_r11l_solve.json,
experiment_3981_*.json and experiment_3993_*.json record duration_s: 0.0
(their writers round(...,1), so any run under 50ms quantizes to 0.0), which
fails the corrected substrate's 0.01s floor. Whether 0.0 is a rounding
artifact of an honest fast run or a real anomaly needs a judgement; a
correction that swaps one lint error for another lands half-corrected, per
the e0d69d1e30 precedent. exp3981's filename is also hook-matched, so its
half-corrected form is uncommittable without --no-verify, which is forbidden.

Blocked-path variants NOT touched: 3981:32,57 and 3993:32 write
'offline_arc_agi3_perception_planner' on the env-unavailable path. No legal
substrate name exists for 'preconditions failed, nothing ran' -- the legal
set has no member for it (the corpus's one 'precondition_blocked_no_inference'
declaration is also illegal). Choosing any legal name there would be a guess;
reported as a legal-set gap instead.

Recovery note, for the record: while this commit sat staged behind two
concurrent-agent blockers (a pending mutation marker, then an unstaged
pre-commit config), a concurrent flow reverted these very files in the
WORKING TREE -- the staged index kept the fix, and the worktree was restored
from it via git checkout-index. The spec scenario below was unstaged at that
moment and was destroyed outright; it is re-appended here. That an
in-flight fix to the record-integrity layer was itself silently reverted by
a sibling workflow is the concurrent-agents-destroy-work incident class,
live, during the repair of the incident class.

Step 6: SCENARIO-HARNESS-5935-RETIRED-WRITER-SUBSTRATE-DOES-NOT-RETURN +
tests/python/test_arc_writer_substrate_regression.py. AST-based, so the
comments that NAME the retired string do not fire -- only a real string
constant does. Mutation-proved this session: reverting the 3954 writer fix
turned the suite RED (1 failed); restoring turned it GREEN (2 passed).

